      "title": "Rolling Updates and Readiness Gating",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 0,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Rolling Updates and Readiness Gating",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. How a Rolling Update Works",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Default strategy is ==RollingUpdate==",
                "A new **ReplicaSet** scales up, the old one scales down",
                "Pods are replaced gradually, so there is no full outage"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Setting",
                "Meaning",
                "Default"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`maxSurge`",
                  "Extra pods above desired",
                  "25%, rounded up"
                ],
                [
                  "`maxUnavailable`",
                  "Pods allowed below desired",
                  "25%, rounded down"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Zero-Downtime Setup",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "yaml",
              "lines": [
                "strategy:",
                "  type: RollingUpdate",
                "  rollingUpdate:",
                "    maxSurge: 1",
                "    maxUnavailable: 0"
              ],
              "note": "new pod must be Ready before an old one goes"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`maxSurge: 0` + `maxUnavailable: 1` needs no extra pods",
                "Capacity drops by one during the rollout"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Readiness Gating",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "A new pod is ==available== only after it passes readiness",
                "If it never passes, the rollout stalls and old pods keep serving"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "No readiness probe: pods are Ready at container start, so a broken build rolls out fully",
                "Port-only probe passes while dependencies are down",
                "Probe real dependencies (DB, cache) in the readiness endpoint",
                "`progressDeadlineSeconds` (default 600s) marks a stuck rollout failed"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Mark stuck rollouts",
              "text": "Set `minReadySeconds` and a suitable `progressDeadlineSeconds`; no automatic rollback happens."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Helm Charts and Per-Environment Values",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Helm Charts and Per-Environment Values",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Chart and Release",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Chart== = `Chart.yaml` + `values.yaml` + `templates/`",
                "==Release== = one installed instance of a chart",
                "Revision history is stored in cluster **Secrets**"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Values and Precedence",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Go templates read `.Values`; defaults live in `values.yaml`",
                "One `values-<env>.yaml` per env, only the ==differences==",
                "Typical: replicas, resources, ingress host"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "helm upgrade --install app ./chart \\",
                "  -f values-prod.yaml \\",
                "  --set image.tag=1.4.2"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "values.yaml",
                    "sub": "lowest",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "-f files",
                    "sub": "later wins",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "--set",
                    "sub": "highest",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Preview and Gotchas",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Command",
                "Use"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`helm template`",
                  "render locally"
                ],
                [
                  "`helm lint`",
                  "check the chart"
                ],
                [
                  "`helm diff upgrade`",
                  "plugin: show changes"
                ],
                [
                  "`helm upgrade --install --atomic --wait`",
                  "auto-rollback on failure"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 3
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Secrets in values files: use external or sealed secrets",
                "Unpinned tags like `latest`",
                "Copy-pasted full values files drift",
                "`--set` on a list replaces the ==whole list=="
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Per env",
              "text": "Pin the tag, keep only differences, deploy with ==--atomic=="
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "GitOps with Argo CD and Flux",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "GitOps with Argo CD and Flux",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. The GitOps Loop",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Git is the ==single source of truth== for desired state",
                "In-cluster controller ==pulls== and reconciles continuously",
                "CI never runs `kubectl apply` on the cluster"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "CI",
                    "sub": "build image",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Config repo",
                    "sub": "new tag",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Controller",
                    "sub": "pulls",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Cluster",
                    "sub": "reconciled",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Argo CD vs Flux",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "yaml",
              "lines": [
                "spec:",
                "  source:",
                "    repoURL: git@github.com:org/config.git",
                "    path: apps/web",
                "    targetRevision: main",
                "  syncPolicy:",
                "    automated: {prune: true, selfHeal: true}"
              ],
              "note": "Argo CD Application"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Argo CD",
                "Flux"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Resources",
                  "`Application`",
                  "`GitRepository` + `Kustomization` / `HelmRelease`"
                ],
                [
                  "UI",
                  "Web UI: Synced / OutOfSync, health",
                  "None, CLI and CRDs"
                ],
                [
                  "Strength",
                  "App-centric, multi-cluster",
                  "Lighter, image-update automation"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Gotchas",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`kubectl edit` on live cluster is reverted by ==selfHeal==",
                "==prune== deletes resources removed from Git"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Ship and roll back",
              "text": "CI only builds the image and commits the new tag. Roll back with ==git revert==, not kubectl."
            },
            {
              "type": "sidebox",
              "title": "Interview Point",
              "items": [
                "**Push or pull?** Controller pulls; CI holds no cluster access.",
                "**Manual drift?** selfHeal reverts it.",
                "**Rollback?** git revert the config commit."
              ],
              "ink": "orange"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Canary Releases with Service Mesh or Argo Rollouts",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Canary Releases with Service Mesh or Argo Rollouts",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Canary with Rollouts",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Canary==: 5% → 25% → 50% → 100%, promote if metrics {green:healthy}",
                "Plain Deployment: traffic follows ==pod count==, no exact split"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "yaml",
              "lines": [
                "kind: Rollout",
                "strategy:",
                "  canary:",
                "    steps:",
                "    - setWeight: 10",
                "    - pause: {duration: 5m}",
                "    - setWeight: 50"
              ],
              "note": "Rollout CRD replaces Deployment"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`kubectl argo rollouts get rollout app`",
                "`kubectl argo rollouts promote app`",
                "`kubectl argo rollouts abort app`"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Routers and Analysis",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Router",
                "Weights via"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Istio",
                  "VirtualService"
                ],
                [
                  "Linkerd",
                  "SMI"
                ],
                [
                  "NGINX",
                  "canary annotations"
                ],
                [
                  "None",
                  "replica ratio"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Rollouts drives routers via `trafficRouting`",
                "`AnalysisTemplate`: Prometheus error rate, latency",
                "Failure means {red:auto-abort} and rollback",
                "==Blue-green==: two full stacks, Service flips at once"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Gotchas and Interview Point",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "No router: weight approximate",
                "Too little traffic: metrics meaningless",
                "Both versions live: keep DB and API backward compatible"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Why not a Deployment?** Traffic follows pod count.",
                "**What stops a bad canary?** Failed AnalysisTemplate.",
                "**Canary vs blue-green?** Gradual share vs full flip."
              ],
              "style": "star"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Rollback with kubectl rollout and Deployment Cheat Sheet",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Rollback with kubectl rollout and Deployment Cheat Sheet",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Inspect and roll back",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "kubectl set image deploy/app app=img:v2",
                "kubectl rollout status deploy/app",
                "kubectl rollout history deploy/app --revision=2",
                "kubectl rollout undo deploy/app --to-revision=1"
              ],
              "note": "undo with no flag goes to the previous revision"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`undo` re-applies the ==old pod template== only",
                "ConfigMap, Secret and scale changes stay as they are"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Pause, restart, history",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`pause`, make several edits, `resume`: ==one rollout== for all",
                "`restart` replaces pods with no spec change"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "kubectl rollout pause deploy/app",
                "kubectl rollout resume deploy/app",
                "kubectl rollout restart deploy/app"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`revisionHistoryLimit` (default ==10==) caps undoable revisions",
                "`kubernetes.io/change-cause` annotation labels history",
                "Helm: `helm rollback app <revision>`; GitOps: ==git revert=="
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Cheat sheet",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Area",
                "Remember"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Zero downtime",
                  "`maxUnavailable: 0` + `maxSurge: 1`, readiness probes"
                ],
                [
                  "Helm",
                  "`-f values-env.yaml` then `--set`; `--atomic`"
                ],
                [
                  "Argo CD",
                  "`selfHeal` + `prune`"
                ],
                [
                  "Canary",
                  "Rollouts steps + AnalysisTemplate"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Mistake",
              "text": "Expecting `undo` to revert ConfigMap or Secret changes."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Check yourself",
      "role": "quiz",
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Check yourself",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "A Deployment has 4 replicas and the default rolling update (25% / 25%). What are the most pods that can exist, and the fewest available, during rollout?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "maxSurge 25% of 4 = 1, rounded up, so at most **5** pods.",
                "maxUnavailable 25% of 4 = 1, rounded down, so at least **3** available."
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "A broken image that crashes on its first DB query was deployed. The Deployment has no readiness probe. Why did the whole rollout finish?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "Without a probe, a pod is Ready as soon as its container starts.",
                "So old pods were removed on schedule and the bad build replaced them all."
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "Argo CD has selfHeal on. Someone runs `kubectl edit` to change replicas from 3 to 6. What happens?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "Argo CD sees drift and reverts it to the 3 in Git.",
                "Change the value in Git instead, and roll back with git revert."
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}